    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10396" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conquīsītor</span></b>  (access. form in
		Plaut. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conquistor</span></b> ; or, acc. to
		Lachm., <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-quaestor</span></b> ),
			ōris, m.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Milit. t. t.</b>, <i>a recruiting
				officer</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Mil. 25, 67</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Att. 7,
				21, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 21, 11, 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">30, 7, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Merc. 3, 4, 80</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In a theatre, <i>a claqueur</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plaut. Am. prol. 65</span></i> and 82.</div>
